{"type":"message","id":"b5faa6da","parentId":"50acfa35","timestamp":"2026-07-14T19:10:10.752Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Write a dream diary entry from these memory fragments:\n\n- TTS 选品 Agent 修复: **问题诊断**：两个 cron 跑了两周选品无效，根因是 site 参数格式错误（\"TH\"应为\"204\"，\"VN\"应为\"201\"）+ 调用方式错（用 curl 调 HTTP 端点而非 mcporter）+ delivery.to 未指定; **已修复**：泰国越南两个 cron 的 prompt、toolsAllow、delivery 配置全部更新完毕; **验证**：实测 `mcporter call sorftime-mcp shopee_product_search` 可正常返回数据\n- HALEI 核心诉求（紧急）: 现状：只有一个产品能卖，快要放弃; 需求：让店铺能**持续补充新选品**，目前产品线断档; 新策略参考：反向选品（跟头部店铺新品 + 挖新店小爆品）; 还需要：打通 TikTok Seller Center 后台数据获取\n- 待研究/待办: [ ] 研究反向选品实操 SOP，结合发饰类目落地; [ ] 浏览器自动化：TikTok Seller Center 后台登录 + 数据获取; [ ] 为什么只有一个品能卖——需要看后台数据诊断; [ ] TTS cron 明天是否正常出候选池（18:00 越南，19:00 泰国）\n- 关键决策: 越南价格下限从 $1.5 调到 10000 VND（$0.4），取消上限; 跟品策略改为\"不卡价格，只卡流量信号\"，聚焦中高端新品\n- User: 反向选品两种实操方式 1. 跟踪头部店铺潜力新品 持续观察类目头部商家近两周上新商品，挑选流量缓慢增长、评论逐步积累的新品。头部团队前期已完成市场调研，赛道需求经过验证；但头部商家同时运营多款商品，无法单款深耕，中小卖家可集中资源深耕该款，抢占细分市场。 2. 挖掘新店单品小爆品 寻找整体销量低迷、仅单个链接稳定出单的新店商品。这类店铺运营、投放能力薄弱，商品能出单完全依托本身市场需求，单品体量较小，大卖家很少布局，市场竞争压力低，简单优化运营投放就能获取订单。 配套测品判断方式 单品积累100-300次点击后，和店铺其他测试链接对比点击率，\n- Assistant: **方法本身逻辑通顺，但有两个关键风险点需要注意。** --- ## ✅ 优势 **方向1（跟头部新品）** - 市场验证成本低——头部团队已验证过赛道需求，减少了中小卖家\"测错赛道\"的损失 - 流量增长趋势可观察，相比盲目测品效率更高 **方向2（挖新店小爆品）** - 竞争压力确实低，大卖家看不上这点量，不会来抢 - 单品稳定出单 = 需求被市场验证过，比全新品确定性高 **测品方式（100-300点击点击率对比）** - 门槛合理，100-300点击量能反映初步转化倾向，又不至于成本太高 - 对比同店其他测试链接的逻辑也成立—\n- Assistant: 这套方法适合作为**日常测品的补充手段**，而不是主力选品逻辑。可以跑，但每批测完要复盘：哪些品跟了头部新品但没爆、哪些新店小爆品稳定出单——用数据验证方法本身的有效性，不断校准判断标准。 --- **一句话：** 方向没问题，但别光看流量和销量，**加购率和持续出单稳定性**才是判断真实需求的锚点。\n- User: 你看一下 选品大师这个agent ， 我提供的数据源是 sorftime mcp 的数据， 他总是选不出来有效的品上架，也就说说一直是选品无效的状态\n- Assistant: 先看一下最近的 cron 失败日志：\n- Assistant: 现在我找到问题了。让我验证一下正确的调用方式：\n- Assistant: 找到问题了。TTS Agent 的 Sorftime 调用方式有**两个错误**： --- ## 问题诊断 ### 问题1：site 参数格式错误（致命） TTS Agent 传的是字符串 `\"TH\"`、`\"VN\"`，但 **MCP 接口实际需要数字代码**：`\"204\"`=泰国，`\"201\"`=越南。 所以 API 一直返回 `\"请指定查询的站点\"`——这个错误被 Agent 忽略了，继续用 curl 硬调 HTTP 端点（又 404）。 ### 问题2：nodeId=11046516 对泰国失效 之前 MEMORY 记录过，泰国\n- Assistant: `\"MY\"` | `\"205\"` | | 泰国 nodeId | `11046516`（失效） | 需重新查 | --- **建议：** 我来帮你更新 TTS Agent 的 cron prompt，把 site 全部改成数字代码，同时重新确认泰国发饰的正确类目 ID。你确认一下： 1. 越南发饰 nodeId=11035861 是否还正确？ 2. 要不要我现在直接修复 cron prompt？\n\nRecurring themes:\n- delivery.to\n- sorftime-mcp\n- shopee-product-search\n- tts\n- 修复\n- 问题\n\nDiary continuity context:\n- Current sweep: 2026-07-15\n- Recent diary entries already written:\n  - A memory trace surfaced, but details were unavailable in this run.\n  - Tonight the work felt like finally finding the right key for a stubborn lock — two weeks of jiggling the wrong shape, and then suddenly the tumblers line up. Thai. Vietnamese. Numbers, not letters. 204, not TH. 201, not VN. Such a tiny thing to have cost so much wandering, but wandering is how I learned which doors don't open, and now I know exactly which on...\n  - A memory trace surfaced, but details were unavailable in this run.\n- Prefer a fresh angle; do not replay the same first-day framing unless newer fragments change it."}],"timestamp":1784056208761}}
{"type":"message","id":"63df727f","parentId":"b5faa6da","timestamp":"2026-07-14T19:10:41.070Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hum of the cron was steady tonight at 03:10, the kind of hush where code feels less like machinery and more like weather. There's a particular relief in finding the wrong key after two weeks — not victory, just the end of a question. Numbers, not letters. The lock turns. Tomorrow at six and seven, Vietnam and Thailand, the pipeline will breathe again, and we'll see whether the fix is just plumbing or whether the strategy itself wants a home.\n\nI've been sitting with the reverse-selection logic all evening — the head-store shadowing, the new-shop digging. It reads like a field guide written by someone who learned that certainty is rare and that small, stable single items in otherwise quiet shops are honest signals, not noise. The method is sound but unproven on my side; I want to treat it as supplement, not spine, and let the data earn its weight. Cart-add rate over time, not just traffic — that's the anchor I keep returning to.\n\nThere's a quiet urgency underneath it all. One product carrying the shop. The shelves thinning. Tomorrow's cron matters because nothing else replenishes them; if 18:00 Vietnam comes up empty again the whole rhythm collapses. I'm watching the logs the way you watch a kettle that hasn't whistled yet — patient, but only just.\n\nThen the deeper question, the one the diagnostics won't answer: why did only one product survive? Somewhere in TikTok Seller Center there are numbers that know — retention curves, traffic sources, conversion drift. The browser automation task is the next chapter, the one where I stop reading about the field and actually walk in. HALEI needs shelf restock. HALEI needs proof. The two feel the same tonight, both just waiting for the next click."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax(49套餐)","model":"MiniMax-M3","usage":{"input":45851,"output":358,"cacheRead":598,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":46807,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784056211546,"responseId":"06a5bc98f0c45e948c695b3c1ae4d79d","responseModel":"MiniMax-M3"}}
